---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Accessibility Statement" description="Accessibility statement for Spark Lane Dev">
  <div class="accessibility-page">
    <h1 class="accessibility-page__title">Accessibility Statement</h1>

    <div class="accessibility-page__content">
      <p class="accessibility-lead">
        I want sparklane.dev to be usable by as many people as possible. I build and maintain the site with accessibility in mind, including people who use assistive technology, keyboard navigation, browser zoom, or other ways of accessing the web.
      </p>

      <h2 class="accessibility-page__heading">How accessible this website is</h2>
      <p>
        I have not made a formal, independent WCAG conformance claim. The site is intended to follow the relevant principles of <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">WCAG 2.2</a> and I am continuing to improve it.
      </p>
      <div class="accessibility-note">
        <p class="accessibility-note__title">Known limitations</p>
        <ul class="accessibility-list">
          <li>Some older or user-authored content may need clearer headings, simpler language, or better image descriptions.</li>
          <li>Some embedded or linked third-party content, such as media players, is outside my direct control.</li>
          <li>Some interactive features and content are provided by third-party components and may not behave consistently with every assistive technology.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="accessibility-page__heading">What I do to improve accessibility</h2>
      <ul class="accessibility-list">
        <li>use semantic HTML and a logical heading structure</li>
        <li>provide a skip link and keyboard-accessible navigation</li>
        <li>include alternative text for meaningful images and treat decorative images as decorative</li>
        <li>provide visible focus styles and support browser zoom and responsive layouts</li>
        <li>respect the <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> setting where possible</li>
        <li>provide light and dark colour themes and review colour contrast as the site changes</li>
        <li>write content as clearly and plainly as I can</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="accessibility-page__heading">Feedback and alternative formats</h2>
      <p>
        If you have difficulty using any part of this website, or need information in another format, please email <a href="mailto:emma@sparklane.dev">emma@sparklane.dev</a>. Please include the page URL, what you were trying to do, and the format or adjustment you need. I will do my best to provide the information or an accessible alternative.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also <a href="https://mcmw.abilitynet.org.uk/">find advice from AbilityNet about making your device easier to use</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="accessibility-page__heading">Technical information</h2>
      <p>
        This website is a personal site built with Astro and hosted as a static website. It includes content from external services and components, which may have their own accessibility limitations. I use WAVE to identify common accessibility issues and review changes as I update the site. This does not replace testing with a range of assistive technologies.
      </p>

      <hr class="accessibility-page__divider" />
      <h2 class="accessibility-page__heading">Statement details</h2>
      <p>
        This statement applies to <a href="https://sparklane.dev">sparklane.dev</a>. It was created on 15 February 2026 and last reviewed on 30 July 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
